original_source_statement_tex:
\label{lemma-surjective-graded-rings-generated-degree-1-map-proj}
With hypotheses and notation as in Lemma \ref{lemma-morphism-proj} above.
Assume $A_d \to B_d$ is surjective for $d \gg 0$ and that $A$ is generated
by $A_1$ over $A_0$. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $U(\psi) = Y$,
\item $r_\psi : Y \to X$ is a closed immersion, and
\item the maps $\theta : r_\psi^*\mathcal{O}_X(n) \to \mathcal{O}_Y(n)$
are isomorphisms.
\end{enumerate}

statement:
\begin{reference}
\cite[II, Proposition 2.8.10]{EGA}
\end{reference}
Let $A,B$ be graded rings, $\psi:A\to B$ a graded ring map, $X=\operatorname{Proj}(A)$ and $Y=\operatorname{Proj}(B)$. Put $U(\psi)=\bigcup_{f\in A_+\text{ homogeneous}}D_+(\psi(f))\subset Y$ and let $r_\psi:U(\psi)\to X$ and $\theta_\psi$ be the canonical morphism and graded-sheaf map of the source lemma. 
Assume there exists a ring map $R \to A_0$ and a ring map
$R \to R'$ such that $B = R' \otimes_R A$. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $U(\psi) = Y$,
\item the diagram
$$
\xymatrix{
Y = \text{Proj}(B) \ar[r]_{r_\psi} \ar[d] &
\text{Proj}(A) = X \ar[d] \\
\Spec(R') \ar[r] &
\Spec(R)
}
$$
is a fibre product square, and
\item the maps $\theta : r_\psi^*\mathcal{O}_X(n) \to \mathcal{O}_Y(n)$
are isomorphisms.
\end{enumerate}

